WEBVTT

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.910
Hello, kids!

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.070
How are you?!

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:16.240
I'm Uramichi Oniisan,
your gymnast Oniisan!

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.370
It's time for <i>Together with Maman</i>!

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:25.250
Okay, kids! Come gather around me!

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.090
Doesn't he seem even more
hyper than usual?

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.300
It's painful to watch.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.430
Uramichi Oniisan has his
ups and downs, so...

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:35.600
Hmm...

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:41.730
Okay! Let's start the fun, amusing,
and exciting ABC exercise!

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.060
Everyone! Follow my lead, okay?!

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.200
See? It's starting to look bad.

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:52.860
Well, everyone!

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.370
Yeah! There's something
I want you to hear!

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:59.200
Oh? He might be feeling better.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.670
You know... When you get to be my age,

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:06.800
the allocation of your mood throughout
the day is pretty much set in stone,

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.550
perhaps to protect your body
from collapsing by accidentally

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.800
going beyond your limits.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.140
But that feature can sometimes
cause a malfunction.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.550
Err...

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:20.140
As you can see, I'm allocating
my mood wrongly today.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.850
At this rate, about 70% of my energy
will be used up just in the morning.

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.900
You'll die, Oniisan.

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.320
But don't worry!

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.530
I can pull this off because I'm an adult!

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:34.950
Because I'm an adult...!

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.450
I don't wanna be an adult like that.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:07.950
"Life Lessons with Uramichi Oniisan"

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:11.340
Hey, kids! Gather around!

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.680
All right! Don't push the others, okay?

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:19.300
Hm?

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.890
Well...?

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:24.180
Kazuki-<i>kun</i>. What's wrong?

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.310
You seem down. Come play with us!

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.020
I see. You don't want to, huh?

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:36.490
Could you try explaining
why you don't want to?

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:40.950
Hm?

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:45.160
Oniisan. He's been like that the
whole time. Why don't we just let him be?

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.870
He just ignores us.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.670
Forget him! Let's play already!

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:51.540
Kazuki-<i>kun</i>.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:57.880
You know... I, too, often feel like
not doing anything at all.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:01.510
But people won't leave me alone.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:05.390
It's not because they like me.

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.480
It's because, if someone
isn't a team player,

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:12.480
you can no longer
conduct business smoothly.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:17.690
In order to live to see tomorrow and also
to be able to go home as soon as possible,

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:22.200
you kids need to learn to cooperate, okay?

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:26.450
Kazuki-<i>kun</i>.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:31.630
One day, you'll surely realize
that you were very lucky

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.380
that people left you alone.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:34.920
I-I'll play.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.550
Oh, really?!

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:40.220
All right! Hey, everyone!
Kazuki-<i>kun </i>wants to play, too!

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:43.390
This is great! Let him join you, okay?!

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:44.800
Okay!

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.720
Oh, speaking of joining them,

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.270
do you think we should call out
Usao-<i>kun </i>and Kumao-<i>kun</i>?

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:52.150
What?

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:56.020
In my opinion, we don't have
to call them out at all, though.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:58.740
W-We don't have to?

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:00.240
Please call them out.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:04.820
Yeah? You're such a good boy,
caring about your friends.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:09.870
Everyone! Let's call out to
Usao-<i>kun </i>and Kumao-<i>kun </i>loudly!

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.410
One, two...!

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.540
Usao-<i>kun</i>!

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:16.750
Kumao-<i>kun</i>!

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:20.380
Hey, Kumatani. Please.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:23.180
I'll return it next month for sure!

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:24.220
Get off me.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:27.260
If I can't pay my rent,
I'll really be in big trouble.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.930
They might kick me out, you know!

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.100
Heavy.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.980
It's your own fault in the first place!

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:36.440
If you play pachinko
and mahjong all the time,

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.230
you're sure to run out
of money at some point.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:39.900
But...

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:42.030
Don't "but" me!

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:45.370
Besides, you still owe me
the 20,000 yen I lent you before.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:46.580
Oh... You still remember that?

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:47.870
Just camp out.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.330
Hey, Kumatani.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:54.790
We're friends, right? Best friends, right?

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:58.000
Those're the last words
you should use at a time like this.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.500
I'm sorry!

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:01.840
Why don't you just borrow
from Uramichi-<i>san</i>?

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.930
Do you want me dead?

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:08.310
Ahh, seriously, I wanna go back
to when we lived in a college dorm.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:12.430
It was easy to get together
for drinking then, too.

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:17.940
It's kind of pain to go to Uramichi-<i>san</i>'s
place because it's kinda far.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:21.190
But I don't recall asking you
to come over even once...

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:23.360
Hm? What?!

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:27.740
...though we've been telling you
to come out many times for a while now.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:30.330
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! We'll be right out!

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:33.410
Also... lend me money
for this month's rent, please.

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:36.330
You've got some nerve
asking that in this situation.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.130
Everyone!

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:44.510
Here are your friends,
Usao-<i>kun </i>and Kumao-<i>kun</i>!

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:48.430
One of them might suddenly
be gone tomorrow, though.

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:52.850
If he is, he's just hibernating,
so you don't have to worry, okay?

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:56.350
Please, anything but firing me.

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:59.400
Usao-<i>kun </i>and Kumao-<i>kun</i>. Where do you live?

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:01.570
We live in a forest, <i>kuma</i>!

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:07.990
But Usao-<i>kun </i>is a bad boy, so it seems
like he's about to get kicked out, <i>kuma</i>.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:09.070
Poor thing.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:09.950
Are you gonna be okay?

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:12.410
It'll be tough for Usao-<i>kun</i>.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:17.370
I-If you get kicked out, I'll ask
my mommy if we can keep you.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:23.710
Me, too. If that doesn't work, I'll build
your house next to Pochi's in our yard!

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:25.090
Me, too! Me, too!

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:26.970
I'll ask my mommy, too!

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:28.130
Everyone...

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:31.850
What?

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:34.640
Is Uramichi-<i>san </i>moved for real?

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:37.390
Seriously? Is he okay?

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:41.150
These kind, innocent children
may waste money on pachinko.

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:43.400
Or they may get drunk
after being rejected in a group date

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:45.940
and end up sleeping in the street
and getting questioned by police.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:50.740
When I think that they might
become like that in the future,

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:51.950
tears just well up.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.950
Why is he so specific?

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:56.710
I feel guilty, like the time
I made my mom cry.

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:59.040
He's talking about you.

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:01.960
Thank you for your good work!

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:04.380
I've got detox tea. Would you like some?

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:07.340
Yes! Yes! Did you make it
yourself by any chance?

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:09.090
Uramichi-<i>kun</i>. You're coming to
the drinking party after this, right?

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:12.350
Yes, I did! I've gotten into it lately.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:12.350
Err... If possible, I'd like to go home.

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:16.640
Gee... You're good at joking.

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:16.640
So, what're you gonna do about your rent?

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:18.270
Hmm...

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:20.190
Ah!

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:22.060
Iketeru-<i>kun</i>. Iketeru-<i>kun</i>.

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.480
Yes?

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:26.030
Lend me some money, please?

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:27.030
Sure.

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:29.320
No, no, no, no!

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.490
You worry me so much.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:33.240
You really do.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:36.160
What kind of upbringing did you have?

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:37.200
What?

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:41.670
Kids! Always try to plan ahead,
and be organized, okay?

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.380
He wrapped it up suddenly...

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:47.170
...even though nothing has been resolved.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.260
Uramichi Oniisan!

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:55.260
Don't you think that things like

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:58.810
logic and sound arguments
aren't useful in society at all?

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:01.310
You're pretty tired, too, aren't you?

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:03.690
Look who's talking.

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:04.350
Yeah.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:06.520
Ah... Sorry.

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:09.360
Yeah.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.240
Overlooking despicable things
or things you can't agree with...

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:16.160
I don't want to be corrupted like that.

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:19.870
What? Do I look corrupted?

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:23.500
I don't know. But you do look like
you're putting up with a lot of things.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:27.250
Well, if I say I'm not, that'd be a lie.

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:29.170
I hurt my lower back yesterday, too.

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:30.970
What were you doing?

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:33.010
I was weightlifting absentmindedly,

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:35.640
and by the time I noticed,
my lower back was hurting.

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:38.770
The barbell was twice
as heavy as my usual one.

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:40.390
That happens a lot, right?

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:42.390
No, normally it doesn't.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:45.230
What? It doesn't?

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:51.780
Anyway, I can push myself for the
children who look forward to the program.

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:55.700
When I see their smiles,
I forget about the pains in my body.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:00.000
Uramichi-<i>san</i>...

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:07.340
Hello, kids! How are you?!

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.500
I'm Uramichi Oniisan.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.420
Are you doing fine today as well?!

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:12.250
Hey.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:13.300
Hm?

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:15.260
Yeah?

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:16.890
Pick me up.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.100
Oh... no...

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:22.680
Just imagining it gives me a back pain.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:32.320
Hey. Hurry up.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:39.450
O-Okay! I'll pick you up!

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:40.910
Ow!

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:42.000
That looks fun!

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:45.750
--Me, too!
--Pick me up, too!

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:50.500
Hey, Kumatani!

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:51.670
Listen! Yesterday...

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:52.550
No.

00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:58.090
I went to a girls' bar. The girls
who work there loved my stories!

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:03.270
They said I was funny! It's like
my time has come, you know!

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:05.770
So, whether you work at a
girls' bar or have an office job,

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:08.520
I guess you won't be successful
without some servility.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:09.560
What?

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:12.820
Unless you yield to your
company's unreasonableness,

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:16.070
or you pretend that you're amused
by a shitty customer's shitty stories,

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:18.410
you can't go on living, huh...?

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:21.870
I think the girls' bar's girls are always
fighting the impulse to punch

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:26.620
the shitty customer who thinks that he's
making them laugh with his shitty stories.

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:29.040
I really do respect them.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.250
Wait. Stop talking like that.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:34.800
There's no servility in
girls' bars to begin with.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:36.010
Ah...

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:41.180
Kumao-<i>kun</i>. What do you
mean by "servility"?

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:45.730
I'm only five years old, so I don't
understand difficult things, <i>kuma</i>.

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:48.060
Would a 31-year-old know?

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.650
Yeah, a 31-year-old would know, <i>kuma</i>.

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:51.940
Thank you!

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:57.900
Uramichi Oniisan.
What does "servility" mean?

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:02.490
It means... to imagine...
another's feelings.

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:05.200
It sounds nice, right?

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:10.960
But you have no choices or autonomy
before extensive authority.

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:14.050
So, it actually means that you should
cleverly curry favor with big shots,

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:16.840
if you want to live to see tomorrow.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:19.550
In short, what you're doing right now?

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:21.050
Right.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:24.180
Since you kids are
still small, there are times

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:24.180
I got bored of it.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:29.020
when you feel that adults are talking
about something difficult, right?

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:30.600
--Yep, yep.
--Yeah!

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:35.610
The truth is, adults aren't really
talking about anything difficult.

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:38.950
Out of self-protection,
they're just trying to baffle others

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:44.910
by paraphrasing simple things
to make them sound complex.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:49.750
Long speeches can diminish people's
concentration as well as attention, so...

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:53.460
It's like when you kids try to change
the subject while being scolded

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:58.050
in order to reduce the
level of anger towards you.

00:12:58.050 --> 00:13:02.720
You'll be learning many difficult words.
I sometimes think that

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:09.680
most of those difficult words exist
so that people can give good excuses.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:12.270
I wonder when we're supposed to go out.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:13.230
Yesterday...

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:14.110
Hm?

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:16.940
Uramichi-<i>san </i>took me out to eat <i>yakiniku</i>.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:19.740
What? That's not fair.
I wanted to go, too.

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:24.740
He was saying a venomless,
nice thing, which he rarely does.

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:28.790
Since it was such an ordinary thing, and
normally, he'd never say anything like it,

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:31.330
Pick me up one more time!

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:31.330
I thought it was a little creepy,
to be honest.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:36.130
But I also think that he was
speaking from his heart.

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:40.720
Even though he's so corrupted
that he thinks nice words are all lies...

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:44.340
...and no matter how suppressed
he is by society and authority,

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.140
he's desperately trying every day

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:52.270
at least to not lose the small amount
of conscience he has as a gymnast Oniisan.

00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:54.350
Uramichi-<i>san</i>...

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:59.940
I was just speculating,
but I'm not far off... right?

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:03.240
I feel like he's concerned
about me in a mortifying way.

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:06.580
Invite me for <i>yakiniku</i>, too!

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:08.740
Thank you for your good work!

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:11.450
Bye-bye!

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.580
Bye-bye!

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:17.790
It was nerve-wracking, wasn't it?

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:22.220
Yeah. I never imagined that
the GM's family members were here.

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:26.640
What? Are that boy and
his mother the GM's family?

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:30.180
Yeah. Don't tell me... you didn't know?

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:33.060
The mother told me earlier
that she was a fan of mine

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:37.770
and asked me to give her
my personal contact info.

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:43.360
So, I turned her down...
by saying that I don't do that.

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.660
Err...

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:46.950
Um...

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:49.490
Thank you very much for everything.

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:51.370
Ah... yeah.

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:53.540
Take care, okay?

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:56.880
She said, "He's unexpectedly reserved,
and I actually like it,"

00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:58.710
and forgave him.

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:09.180
Hello! We're giving a free brain age test!

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:12.350
We're giving a balloon
to every test taker!

00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:14.940
How about giving it a try?!

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:18.400
We're giving a free brain age test!

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.440
We'll give you a balloon!

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.570
You'll get a balloon!

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:23.860
No thank you.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:26.200
Don't you wanna know your brain's age?

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:27.700
I'm on my way to work, so...

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:30.240
It won't take much time.
Just a little bit!

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:32.910
This is a Father's Day promotion,
so it's free right now!

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:36.830
There are many families with children
around. Why me? I'm not even a father.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:39.250
Hurry up and sit down! It's starting now.

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:42.460
Let's begin.

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:46.680
Please follow the instructions
and press a button.

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:48.550
Please lose at paper, rock, scissors.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:49.680
What?

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.640
That's incorrect.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:55.430
Please lose.

00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:58.980
That's incorrect.

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:00.690
Please lose.

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:01.190
What?

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:02.360
That's incorrect.

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:03.820
Please lose.

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:04.310
Hm?

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:05.610
That's incorrect.

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:07.030
Please lose.

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:07.520
What?

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:08.530
That's incorrect.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:10.490
"Your brain age is..."
"91 years old"
"Please work hard on training your brain."

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:20.250
--Daddy. Is Uramichi Oniisan really coming?
--Hey, Dad! Here! This way!

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:18.990
"Jump Out!
Together with Papan"

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:22.290
So that's what happened.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:26.260
She definitely likes me! I'm sure of it!

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:28.260
Uramichi-<i>san</i>. Good morning.

00:16:28.260 --> 00:16:32.350
Ah! Uramichi-<i>san</i>! G'morning! Hm?

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:36.100
Morning. Do you want a balloon?

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:37.600
No thanks.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:39.350
In this job, it's important
to look good with balloons,

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:41.060
and yet, to think you
look this bad with one...

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:41.640
Say what?

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:43.570
Nothing!

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:45.900
Please get ready!

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:49.280
Ah... Hey, let's get
going already, Uramichi-<i>san</i>.

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:56.080
Oh, yeah, Uramichi-<i>san</i>.

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:58.910
Did you see the new <i>Man-Eating Salmon</i>?

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:02.830
Yeah, I did. The scene where
they caught the salmon climbing up

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:04.880
the huge flowing <i>somen </i>waterfall was good.

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:08.380
What's so fun about watching
those weird movies?

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:11.010
Usahara. Hurry up and change.

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:13.090
You, too, right, Uramichi-<i>san</i>?

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:16.060
By the way, aren't those two
singers here today?

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:18.810
I heard that they have
a recording for a new song.

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:22.850
It's time for the
Father's Day special event

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:27.730
"Jump Out! Together with Papan"!

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:31.990
So, kids and families!
Please come and take a seat!

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:35.160
Today, your gymnast Oniisan
and jolly friends

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:39.000
jumped out of their studio
and came to see you!

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.830
Well then, let's have them come out!

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:43.330
Uramichi Oniisan!

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:46.800
Usao-<i>kun</i>! Kumao-<i>kun</i>!

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:51.300
Hello, everyone! How are you?!

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:55.180
We're doing really well!

00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:58.600
If you're balancing your physical
and mental states, even if it's barely,

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:02.020
it means you're doing well!
That's how it is in this modern society!

00:18:02.020 --> 00:18:05.360
Today, we're going to do
the ABC Exercise outside the studi--

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:06.900
Uramichi Oniisan!

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:07.440
Hm?

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:08.690
Hey, hey, Takkun.

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.740
You shouldn't interfere.

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:15.070
But you always tell me that I should
properly say thank you to others.

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:15.910
What?

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:19.660
My dad is always busy, but he made
an exception today and took a day off

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:22.500
to take me to see you, Oniisan.

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:25.710
Because of that, I can
spend time with him today!

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:27.380
Thank you, Oniisan!

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.840
What? Is he crying? Seriously?

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:34.720
What? Why?

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:40.890
Okay! We're now going to show you the
drawings that the kids did of their dads!

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:45.850
Wow! Everyone did a good job drawing!

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:52.400
"Tooru, 4 years old" "Mahiro, 5 years old"

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:48.820
Now, Uramichi Oniisan and friends!

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:51.900
You're going to draw your fathers
for us today, right?

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:55.360
What? That wasn't... in the script.

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:58.200
What? We're drawing, too?

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:02.450
Kids! Would you like to see Oniisan
and friends' fathers, too?

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:03.620
We want to!

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:04.490
Right?!

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:06.630
She's one forceful MC.

00:19:07.710 --> 00:19:11.170
My dad, huh? I wonder
if I can draw him well.

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:14.340
Hey, do you guys even
remember your father's face?

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:17.800
Well... yeah, of course, I do, but...

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:20.140
But when I'm asked to draw him...

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:23.980
Oniisan. What's taking so long
for you to draw your dad?

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:26.520
As you grow older,
you have less opportunities

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:30.480
to pay attention and look
at your father's face.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:32.610
Will I come to dislike him?

00:19:32.610 --> 00:19:36.610
No, you won't.
You'll just feel a little awkward.

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:37.610
Hm?

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:40.450
Done.

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:41.910
I'm done, too.

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:44.450
Hm? Wait. What about your characters?

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:45.330
What?

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:48.880
I'm asking about your
own characters. They're humans.

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:50.290
Ah...

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:54.880
They look like ordinary old guys.

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:59.390
What? Usao-<i>kun</i>. Kumao-<i>kun</i>.
Aren't your dads a bunny and a bear?

00:19:59.390 --> 00:20:01.180
He's totally a bear, <i>kuma</i>!

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:04.980
N-No matter how you look at him,
he's a cute bunny, hop!

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:09.190
I was just thinking too much about my
father who I haven't seen in a long time.

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:12.070
I drew him intently.

00:20:12.070 --> 00:20:14.110
Oh, th-that's right, hop.

00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:17.110
Let's take a look at Oniisan's dad, hop!

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:20.120
Oh, good! He looks relatively normal...

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:21.450
Not!

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:23.490
What?! It looks scary! What's this?

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:24.910
What's going on there?

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.540
My father was strict.

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:31.590
When I was small, if I skipped training,
he'd throw me onto a mat.

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:33.800
Is this you, Uramichi-<i>san</i>?!

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:37.800
My little sister left home at the age
of 16 as if to escape from him.

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:40.260
Oh, so this is your sister, huh?

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:42.430
I didn't know you have a sister.

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:45.850
You don't hate your dad
when he's like that?

00:20:45.850 --> 00:20:48.810
If I hadn't been born as the son
of a father like him,

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:52.360
I'm sure I wouldn't be here, so...

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:55.570
You can only live once, no matter what.

00:20:55.570 --> 00:20:57.820
You sometimes think
that you made a mistake

00:20:57.820 --> 00:21:00.490
even when you don't know
if it really was a mistake.

00:21:00.490 --> 00:21:03.780
But if you can feel that you're happy
in the end, even if it's just a little,

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:07.750
I'm certain that you
didn't make a mistake.

00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:11.920
Whether your parents' mistakes
can be overturned or not

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:16.920
depends on how you kids
live your life in the future.

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:19.380
You may not be able to live
for someone else.

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:25.310
But it'd be nice if you chose to live
in a way in which you don't blame others.

00:22:56.730 --> 00:22:58.610
Good work!

00:22:58.610 --> 00:23:02.820
Uramichi-<i>san</i>! Let's go out for a drink!
You, too, Kumatani! Let's go!

00:23:02.820 --> 00:23:05.570
That's fine, but first,
play rock, paper, scissors with me.

00:23:05.570 --> 00:23:08.490
What? Rock, paper, scissors?

00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:12.660
Listen, go slightly late
and lose on purpose, got it?

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:15.330
Huh? O-Okay.

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:17.540
Ready? One, two, three!

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:18.380
Three.

00:23:18.380 --> 00:23:19.960
One, two, three.

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:20.800
Three.

00:23:20.800 --> 00:23:22.090
Three.

00:23:22.090 --> 00:23:23.380
Three.

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:24.510
Three.

00:23:24.510 --> 00:23:26.010
Three.

00:23:27.930 --> 00:23:31.890
What? What's this game? It's super easy.

00:23:31.890 --> 00:23:34.100
If you're gonna take the balloon,
I'll go out for a drink.

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:36.810
Wh-What? I don't want it.

00:23:36.810 --> 00:23:39.980
Oh, Kumatani! Why don't we play rock,
paper, scissors, and the loser will take--

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:40.820
No way.

00:23:40.820 --> 00:23:43.110
What? Hey, Kumatani. Just once.

00:23:43.110 --> 00:23:44.030
No way.

00:23:44.030 --> 00:23:45.240
Just once!

00:23:45.240 --> 00:23:46.570
No way.
